WEBVTT

00:00:11.570 --> 00:00:13.490
Why didn't you go after him?

00:00:14.320 --> 00:00:17.550
If I'd gone after Jonas, you 
would have been killed by wolves.

00:00:17.550 --> 00:00:18.870
I know that!

00:00:19.370 --> 00:00:22.550
Even so, I didn't want to let him 
have that sugar confection.

00:00:23.270 --> 00:00:24.330
But you...

00:00:24.930 --> 00:00:28.570
You protected me so your
 wing wouldn't be damaged!

00:00:28.570 --> 00:00:30.050
That's all it was, wasn't it?

00:00:30.930 --> 00:00:34.010
I know! I'm not capable of using you!

00:00:34.310 --> 00:00:36.680
I know that! I know!

00:00:37.170 --> 00:00:38.440
I know...

00:00:46.490 --> 00:00:54.510
<i>I don't know how far I can go, but…</i>

00:01:01.200 --> 00:01:03.930
<i>It's all right</i>

00:01:03.930 --> 00:01:07.770
<i>Even alone, I'll be fine, but…</i>

00:01:07.770 --> 00:01:14.270
<i>You know, the truth is
 that no one is alone</i>

00:01:14.270 --> 00:01:20.850
<i>Things like happiness, 
loneliness, and even anxiety…</i>

00:01:20.850 --> 00:01:30.170
<i>We are born to savor all those things</i>

00:01:30.610 --> 00:01:33.820
<i>A single spoonful of sparkles</i>

00:01:33.820 --> 00:01:36.950
<i>Transforms everything into smiles</i>

00:01:37.230 --> 00:01:44.060
<i>That could be what I secretly wished for…</i>

00:01:44.060 --> 00:01:46.750
<i>That miracle</i>

00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:53.710
<i>We're each searching for
 our most precious treasures</i>

00:01:53.710 --> 00:02:00.010
<i>That's what our journey is for</i>

00:02:00.010 --> 00:02:07.140
<i>I don't know how far I can go, but...</i>

00:02:07.140 --> 00:02:15.370
<i>Each moment that passes before me
 shall be spun from hope</i>

00:02:27.680 --> 00:02:28.780
Why...

00:02:29.280 --> 00:02:31.380
He likely intended to enter it 
into the exhibition.

00:02:32.600 --> 00:02:35.590
First, he stole your mother's designs.

00:02:36.360 --> 00:02:38.090
But he was unable to make them work.

00:02:38.740 --> 00:02:43.860
That's why he contrived to steal 
your work and head to Lewiston.

00:02:48.230 --> 00:02:51.190
This is... mine. It's what I lost.

00:02:51.520 --> 00:02:53.830
It was likely Cathy who stole it.

00:02:54.330 --> 00:02:56.280
She has the ability to turn invisible.

00:02:56.670 --> 00:03:01.260
Then, Jonas estimated the amount of 
silver sugar you used to make your piece,

00:03:01.260 --> 00:03:03.480
loaded it into your cart in advance,

00:03:03.480 --> 00:03:06.160
and stole your wagon with 
your finished piece inside.

00:03:09.090 --> 00:03:11.210
How can you know all that?

00:03:11.520 --> 00:03:13.500
That's how humans are.

00:03:14.720 --> 00:03:15.850
I'm returning this.

00:03:20.880 --> 00:03:23.050
The exhibition is the day after tomorrow.

00:03:23.050 --> 00:03:25.940
Jonas will have already reached Lewiston.

00:03:26.680 --> 00:03:28.390
It's too late now.

00:03:29.830 --> 00:03:31.190
And you are satisfied with that?

00:03:32.040 --> 00:03:33.310
Of course I'm not.

00:03:33.680 --> 00:03:35.610
Of course I'm not, 
but there's nothing I can do!

00:03:35.610 --> 00:03:37.940
Even with you here, 
I can't do anything about it!

00:03:38.560 --> 00:03:40.400
So, I'll set you free.

00:03:40.400 --> 00:03:41.860
Go somewhere else!

00:04:00.520 --> 00:04:01.950
And now...

00:04:01.950 --> 00:04:03.290
I'm all alone again.

00:04:05.890 --> 00:04:07.960
I'm sorry, Mama.

00:04:09.130 --> 00:04:11.100
Becoming a silver sugar master...

00:04:11.100 --> 00:04:15.100
and sending your spirit to the heavens 
on Pull Soul Day was my dream.

00:04:15.770 --> 00:04:17.560
And now it won't come true.

00:04:18.670 --> 00:04:20.500
Mama. Mama!

00:04:21.350 --> 00:04:23.080
Why did you die?

00:04:23.640 --> 00:04:25.780
Why did you leave me all alone?

00:04:26.480 --> 00:04:28.780
Why, Mama?!

00:05:05.530 --> 00:05:06.810
How beautiful...

00:05:11.400 --> 00:05:12.940
You're a human, aren't you?

00:05:12.940 --> 00:05:15.530
You're the one who allowed me 
to be born, aren't you?

00:05:15.530 --> 00:05:16.340
What?

00:05:16.830 --> 00:05:18.920
Fairies are born when another's gaze...

00:05:18.920 --> 00:05:22.960
causes the energy within an object 
to condense and take form.

00:05:22.960 --> 00:05:24.410
Challe.

00:05:24.410 --> 00:05:26.260
And you're like me, aren't you?

00:05:26.260 --> 00:05:28.720
I'm Lusul El Min!

00:05:29.210 --> 00:05:32.220
Lusul El Min, go where you like.

00:05:32.730 --> 00:05:34.440
Do not approach humans.

00:05:34.990 --> 00:05:38.560
They capture us, steal our freedom, 
and make us serve them.

00:05:38.890 --> 00:05:41.870
Really? But what about this young lady?

00:05:41.870 --> 00:05:43.390
She's a human, isn't she?

00:05:43.390 --> 00:05:45.240
She's special.

00:05:45.240 --> 00:05:49.660
Now, go. Live as you like in a place 
where humans cannot reach you.

00:05:51.680 --> 00:05:53.130
How kind you are!

00:05:53.130 --> 00:05:54.300
Thank you!

00:06:01.220 --> 00:06:02.630
What does that expression mean?

00:06:02.630 --> 00:06:05.790
Well... Why are you here?

00:06:05.790 --> 00:06:07.480
I returned your wing, didn't I?

00:06:07.480 --> 00:06:10.280
You haven't kept your promise to me.

00:06:10.280 --> 00:06:12.280
I came to have you keep it.

00:06:12.280 --> 00:06:13.350
Promise?

00:06:14.040 --> 00:06:17.730
You promised to give me a sugar confection.

00:06:19.410 --> 00:06:20.920
A sugar confection...

00:06:28.630 --> 00:06:31.820
What's wrong? Will you make it or not?

00:06:35.460 --> 00:06:36.550
I will.

00:06:37.500 --> 00:06:39.200
I did promise, after all!

00:06:39.200 --> 00:06:41.560
I'll make something incredibly beautiful!

00:06:41.560 --> 00:06:42.190
Wait.

00:06:42.190 --> 00:06:44.500
Do not make sugar confections in that state.

00:06:46.470 --> 00:06:47.260
Wear this.

00:06:47.260 --> 00:06:48.090
What?

00:06:48.510 --> 00:06:50.100
It was in the cargo hold.

00:06:50.650 --> 00:06:52.430
No one will mind if you use it, will they?

00:07:00.420 --> 00:07:02.400
<i>I will make a sugar confection.</i>

00:07:11.380 --> 00:07:12.700
<i>For Challe.</i>

00:07:14.820 --> 00:07:17.240
<i>Even if I can't make it to the exhibition...</i>

00:07:18.720 --> 00:07:22.580
<i>Even if he leaves again 
once I give it to him...</i>

00:07:23.680 --> 00:07:25.040
<i>Right now, this is simply...</i>

00:07:25.970 --> 00:07:28.440
<i>for Challe, who came back to me.</i>

00:07:29.820 --> 00:07:34.700
<i>I will make something 
that I feel is beautiful!</i>

00:07:38.180 --> 00:07:39.320
Challe.

00:07:41.620 --> 00:07:42.570
This is it...

00:07:57.050 --> 00:08:00.330
It's very small, but this is my...

00:08:00.880 --> 00:08:04.250
Given who I am right now, 
this is my truest sugar confection.

00:08:06.680 --> 00:08:07.590
Beautiful.

00:08:13.190 --> 00:08:14.750
Thank you.

00:08:14.750 --> 00:08:16.300
Will you accept it?

00:08:28.360 --> 00:08:31.820
Will you allow me to touch your wing?

00:08:33.290 --> 00:08:34.150
Touch it.

00:08:34.540 --> 00:08:35.900
Are you sure?

00:08:46.790 --> 00:08:48.170
It feels so warm.

00:09:15.900 --> 00:09:17.710
Are you satisfied?

00:09:17.710 --> 00:09:18.520
Yes.

00:09:19.080 --> 00:09:21.960
This sugar confection 
belongs to me, doesn't it?

00:09:22.940 --> 00:09:23.690
Yes...

00:09:23.690 --> 00:09:26.420
Then I will do as I please with it.

00:09:28.780 --> 00:09:29.780
Challe?

00:09:30.190 --> 00:09:30.840
Get on.

00:09:31.390 --> 00:09:32.400
We're leaving.

00:09:32.400 --> 00:09:33.950
Huh? Where are we going?

00:09:33.950 --> 00:09:34.910
Lewiston.

00:09:34.910 --> 00:09:35.920
What? What?!

00:09:36.320 --> 00:09:39.140
If we travel through the night, 
we will arrive in the morning.

00:09:39.560 --> 00:09:43.080
You want to become a silver sugar 
master this year, don't you?

00:09:43.080 --> 00:09:43.720
What?

00:09:44.320 --> 00:09:47.240
But the sugar confection 
I was going to enter is...

00:09:47.240 --> 00:09:48.380
You have this.

00:09:50.670 --> 00:09:53.920
If this is your truest work, then enter it.

00:09:53.920 --> 00:09:56.400
If it isn't good enough, 
then you can accept your defeat.

00:09:57.350 --> 00:09:59.700
Why are you doing this for me?

00:10:00.520 --> 00:10:02.480
You returned my wing to me.

00:10:02.480 --> 00:10:04.600
You are no longer my master.

00:10:05.850 --> 00:10:08.730
If that's true, then we can become friends.

00:10:09.660 --> 00:10:10.830
If that's what you wish.

00:10:13.270 --> 00:10:15.880
Challe, is that something you want?

00:10:16.730 --> 00:10:17.910
I don't know.

00:10:24.730 --> 00:10:26.120
Night is coming.

00:10:26.120 --> 00:10:28.390
Will we be able to escape 
the Bloody Highway safely?

00:10:29.600 --> 00:10:31.530
Who do you think I am?

00:10:36.490 --> 00:10:39.000
I wonder which school will get 
the Royal Medal this year.

00:10:39.000 --> 00:10:40.090
It'll be the Mercury school.

00:10:40.090 --> 00:10:41.370
What about the Paige school?

00:10:41.370 --> 00:10:42.740
They're on the decline.

00:10:42.740 --> 00:10:44.650
I'm guessing it'll be the Radcliffe school.

00:10:45.400 --> 00:10:48.840
His Majesty, King Edmond II approaches!

00:10:48.840 --> 00:10:52.590
Wow! Hooray! It's him!

00:10:57.750 --> 00:10:58.600
What's that?

00:10:58.600 --> 00:10:59.400
Watch out!

00:11:01.050 --> 00:11:01.800
Look out!

00:11:01.800 --> 00:11:02.680
Out of the way!

00:11:02.680 --> 00:11:03.890
What is this commotion?

00:11:06.760 --> 00:11:07.890
Stop here, Challe!

00:11:08.270 --> 00:11:09.180
Whoa!

00:11:19.080 --> 00:11:20.910
It appears that the results of

00:11:20.910 --> 00:11:23.160
the Sugar Confectionary Exhibition 
haven't yet been declared!

00:11:23.160 --> 00:11:24.120
Anne!

00:11:24.440 --> 00:11:25.960
I will also enter!

00:11:25.960 --> 00:11:28.430
Sugar Artisan Anne Halford!

00:11:28.430 --> 00:11:29.130
You there!

00:11:28.430 --> 00:11:29.920
No associated school!

00:11:29.130 --> 00:11:30.570
You are brazen!

00:11:30.570 --> 00:11:32.190
Please let me through! I...

00:11:31.350 --> 00:11:33.580
Hey there! Well, well.

00:11:33.920 --> 00:11:37.520
I thought you weren't coming, 
but that was quite the entrance...

00:11:37.520 --> 00:11:38.170
Anne.

00:11:38.170 --> 00:11:39.130
Hugh?

00:11:39.480 --> 00:11:42.430
You know this girl, Mercury?

00:11:42.430 --> 00:11:45.510
Yes. She is, indeed, a sugar artisan.

00:11:45.820 --> 00:11:48.220
<i>Mercury? Hugh Mercury?</i>

00:11:46.030 --> 00:11:48.570
I have ascertained her 
skills with my own eyes.

00:11:48.220 --> 00:11:51.890
<i>The head of the Mercury Workshop school, 
and the current Silver Sugar Viscount?!</i>

00:11:53.160 --> 00:11:54.330
Very well.

00:11:54.330 --> 00:11:56.250
If the Silver Sugar Viscount 
acknowledges her skills,

00:11:56.250 --> 00:11:57.570
then I will authorize her entry.

00:11:57.950 --> 00:12:00.360
Thank you.

00:12:02.800 --> 00:12:04.070
Hey, Anne.

00:12:04.070 --> 00:12:06.700
My clothes suit you quite well.

00:12:06.700 --> 00:12:12.190
That aside... To think you'd enter 
with a piece the size of a child's snack.

00:12:12.190 --> 00:12:14.580
I'm impressed by your nerve.

00:12:15.130 --> 00:12:18.010
You impress me as well, Jonas.

00:12:18.010 --> 00:12:22.720
Entering with someone else's work. 
There should be limits to shamelessness.

00:12:22.720 --> 00:12:25.050
I don't know what you're talking about.

00:12:36.570 --> 00:12:39.730
We now begin the Sugar 
Confectionary Exhibition!

00:12:39.730 --> 00:12:42.680
The greatest sugar artisan in the land...

00:12:42.680 --> 00:12:46.120
shall be granted the title of 
Silver Sugar Master!

00:12:47.530 --> 00:12:51.410
Everyone, His Majesty the King will now 
examine the sugar confections!

00:13:07.060 --> 00:13:08.390
Jonas Anders...

00:13:08.390 --> 00:13:09.900
and Anne Halford.

00:13:09.900 --> 00:13:13.350
Bring your sugar confections 
and approach His Majesty.

00:13:17.330 --> 00:13:19.240
Yes, it's quite strange.

00:13:19.240 --> 00:13:20.020
Mercury.

00:13:21.190 --> 00:13:22.350
What do you think?

00:13:22.350 --> 00:13:26.170
To my eyes, they appear similarly beautiful.

00:13:26.940 --> 00:13:27.990
Indeed.

00:13:28.510 --> 00:13:32.510
They seem as though they might 
have been made by the same artisan,

00:13:32.510 --> 00:13:34.080
given how alike they are.

00:13:35.310 --> 00:13:37.580
Which do you prefer, sire?

00:13:42.820 --> 00:13:44.700
I like this one.

00:13:50.680 --> 00:13:52.680
It seems as though 
it might shatter this instant.

00:13:52.680 --> 00:13:56.170
It's ephemeral, and yet so full of life.

00:13:56.640 --> 00:14:00.230
I have never seen 
such a beautiful sugar sculpture.

00:14:02.440 --> 00:14:06.020
That sugar confection truly is magnificent.

00:14:06.920 --> 00:14:08.990
But, Your Majesty,

00:14:08.990 --> 00:14:11.760
the sugar confection which will be 
the centerpiece of the festival

00:14:11.760 --> 00:14:15.610
must be made large and spectacular.

00:14:15.610 --> 00:14:18.780
Even if she possesses the skills 
to make this small confection,

00:14:18.780 --> 00:14:21.050
we don't know what will happen 
when it comes to a large piece.

00:14:21.890 --> 00:14:23.170
Yes, that is true.

00:14:24.470 --> 00:14:26.940
I have decided. I will make my declaration.

00:14:27.520 --> 00:14:33.260
I award the Royal Medal to the sugar 
confection brought by Jonas Anders.

00:14:36.360 --> 00:14:38.390
Anne Halford, stand aside.

00:14:38.390 --> 00:14:40.570
Jonas Anders, come here.

00:14:40.570 --> 00:14:45.290
His Majesty will examine the three barrels 
of silver sugar you refined,

00:14:45.290 --> 00:14:48.180
so that you may present them to him 
along with the sugar confection.

00:15:01.320 --> 00:15:02.750
Wh-What is this?

00:15:03.730 --> 00:15:05.960
What is the meaning of this, Anders?

00:15:06.320 --> 00:15:09.500
An entire barrel of silver sugar 
is completely missing!

00:15:09.500 --> 00:15:11.420
Th-That can't be!

00:15:11.420 --> 00:15:14.780
Oh, please forgive me, Your Majesty!

00:15:14.780 --> 00:15:19.760
I am but a lowly labor fairy 
in service to Master Jonas Anders!

00:15:19.760 --> 00:15:22.700
My master is so utterly crappy 
at making silver sugar

00:15:22.700 --> 00:15:24.830
that he couldn't make the required amount!

00:15:24.830 --> 00:15:27.790
So, he had me, with my ability 
to use magic which tricks the eyes,

00:15:27.790 --> 00:15:29.720
creep into the barrel to make it appear full!

00:15:29.720 --> 00:15:31.580
<i>Why is Mithril here?</i>

00:15:29.720 --> 00:15:33.640
But the idea of tricking 
Your Majesty was just too, too much!

00:15:32.480 --> 00:15:35.160
<i>It can't be. Did he eat Jonas' silver sugar?</i>

00:15:33.640 --> 00:15:36.620
Please, forgive me, Your Majesty!

00:15:35.470 --> 00:15:36.620
This is a conspiracy!

00:15:36.910 --> 00:15:38.140
Come here!

00:15:38.140 --> 00:15:42.170
That fairy is in service to this 
Anne Halford, who stands before you.

00:15:42.170 --> 00:15:44.880
She wanted to become a silver sugar master,

00:15:44.880 --> 00:15:46.890
so she had that fairy sneak into the barrel!

00:15:46.890 --> 00:15:48.940
Hey! Let Anne go, you scoundrel!

00:15:48.940 --> 00:15:50.510
See? He's confessed!

00:15:50.510 --> 00:15:51.840
They're working together!

00:15:51.840 --> 00:15:54.460
It's true that I know this fairy.

00:15:54.460 --> 00:15:57.640
But I don't know why he's done this.

00:15:57.920 --> 00:15:59.740
Does the why even matter?

00:15:59.740 --> 00:16:02.140
Anne, just tell them the truth!

00:16:02.140 --> 00:16:04.480
Tell them what he did to you!

00:16:07.120 --> 00:16:08.380
Let go!

00:16:08.380 --> 00:16:12.590
The piece that Jonas Anders entered 
and declared as his own...

00:16:12.590 --> 00:16:14.940
is a piece that I made!

00:16:14.940 --> 00:16:17.080
He stole it from me.

00:16:17.080 --> 00:16:18.700
This fairy knew that and so...

00:16:18.700 --> 00:16:20.620
I stole it? That's a lie!

00:16:20.620 --> 00:16:21.960
Let go of Anne!

00:16:21.960 --> 00:16:23.790
Move, you little...

00:16:21.960 --> 00:16:24.010
Are you going to keep lying?

00:16:24.010 --> 00:16:26.000
Silence! You're the liar here!

00:16:26.000 --> 00:16:28.570
Let go! Let go of me!

00:16:26.720 --> 00:16:29.260
Stay still, you little...

00:16:28.570 --> 00:16:31.970
Well, shall we have them 
prove it, Your Majesty?

00:16:30.070 --> 00:16:31.970
Let go!

00:16:34.680 --> 00:16:38.520
Is there a way to discern 
which of them created these works?

00:16:38.520 --> 00:16:40.380
If there is, we should use it.

00:16:40.380 --> 00:16:41.370
Yes, sire.

00:16:41.370 --> 00:16:42.140
Well then...

00:16:42.760 --> 00:16:45.980
I'll have you do the same thing 
you did that night at the Doctor's Inn.

00:16:45.980 --> 00:16:48.610
But this time, there will be a motif.

00:16:51.220 --> 00:16:53.780
This work that His Majesty selected...

00:16:54.270 --> 00:16:56.110
has butterflies on it, doesn't it?

00:16:56.540 --> 00:16:59.960
Make ones identical 
to these here, before His Majesty.

00:16:59.960 --> 00:17:02.360
Then we will be able to tell 
from whose hands these came.

00:17:02.360 --> 00:17:03.080
Understand?

00:17:03.080 --> 00:17:04.830
All right. I'll do it.

00:17:05.570 --> 00:17:06.440
Jonas?

00:17:06.440 --> 00:17:07.790
I-I...

00:17:07.790 --> 00:17:08.620
Begin!

00:17:12.130 --> 00:17:13.050
<i>I can feel it.</i>

00:17:14.070 --> 00:17:16.020
<i>Challe has stayed to watch me.</i>

00:17:17.710 --> 00:17:19.140
<i>I will make a butterfly.</i>

00:17:19.660 --> 00:17:24.010
<i>One that will make Challe happy. 
An incredibly beautiful butterfly.</i>

00:17:24.800 --> 00:17:26.940
<i>I want the wings to be more lustrous.</i>

00:17:27.340 --> 00:17:31.550
<i>Yes, like Challe's wings... so beautiful...</i>

00:17:31.550 --> 00:17:32.400
That's enough!

00:17:37.090 --> 00:17:39.530
Anders' butterfly isn't even 
worth speaking about.

00:17:39.530 --> 00:17:44.510
I-If I don't work alone in a quiet place, 
I can't make anything very well.

00:17:44.510 --> 00:17:47.320
If I could work alone, 
in a quiet place, with enough time...

00:17:47.320 --> 00:17:49.250
You're a disgrace, Jonas!

00:18:02.980 --> 00:18:07.130
Halford's butterfly does resemble those 
of the work that His Majesty chose.

00:18:07.900 --> 00:18:09.270
But they are different.

00:18:10.940 --> 00:18:13.080
What do you mean, Mercury?

00:18:13.800 --> 00:18:20.190
It seems obvious to me which artisan 
created the work I selected.

00:18:20.190 --> 00:18:24.700
Between Halford's butterfly and the butterflies 
on the work Your Majesty chose...

00:18:24.700 --> 00:18:26.860
Which do you prefer, sire?

00:18:30.000 --> 00:18:32.790
Halford's butterfly, of course.

00:18:33.200 --> 00:18:35.630
Compared to the piece 
I chose, it is even more...

00:18:38.660 --> 00:18:42.970
I see. They are not the same. 
That's what you meant.

00:18:43.520 --> 00:18:47.740
That is why I cannot declare 
with certainty which of them made it.

00:18:48.580 --> 00:18:53.580
Yes. It seems that the artisan 
who made the piece I chose...

00:18:53.580 --> 00:18:55.440
is nowhere to be seen.

00:18:56.130 --> 00:18:56.920
Downing!

00:18:56.920 --> 00:18:57.880
Yes, sire.

00:18:57.880 --> 00:18:59.930
There will be no Royal Medal this year.

00:19:00.360 --> 00:19:01.500
That is the end of this.

00:19:02.650 --> 00:19:03.520
What does this mean?

00:19:03.520 --> 00:19:05.180
No Royal Medal?

00:19:05.180 --> 00:19:06.400
Will they pick someone else?

00:19:06.400 --> 00:19:08.500
Does this mean no one's going to 
become a silver sugar master?

00:19:08.500 --> 00:19:10.200
That was a shame.

00:19:11.920 --> 00:19:13.820
My lord Silver Sugar Viscount.

00:19:13.820 --> 00:19:17.590
Hey, now. No need to be so formal. 
Hugh is good enough for me.

00:19:19.120 --> 00:19:21.210
Hugh, why...

00:19:21.210 --> 00:19:25.270
You must have known that piece was mine.

00:19:26.150 --> 00:19:29.430
No, it wasn't. The king 
said so himself, didn't he?

00:19:29.900 --> 00:19:30.900
But...

00:19:31.500 --> 00:19:34.180
Improving your skills worked against you.

00:19:35.960 --> 00:19:38.510
This butterfly that you made just now...

00:19:38.510 --> 00:19:40.610
That wasn't you aping someone else.

00:19:41.200 --> 00:19:44.320
This is clearly your own original work.

00:19:49.380 --> 00:19:51.500
<i>Mama, did you hear that?</i>

00:19:53.140 --> 00:19:54.740
<i>Did you see that?</i>

00:19:58.640 --> 00:20:00.080
Anne Halford.

00:20:00.080 --> 00:20:02.260
Her Majesty has given me a message for you.

00:20:02.990 --> 00:20:03.720
Yes, my lord!

00:20:04.110 --> 00:20:08.240
Next year, she hopes you will bring 
a sugar confection worthy of the festival.

00:20:08.240 --> 00:20:10.890
She is greatly looking forward to it.

00:20:11.280 --> 00:20:13.150
Yes... Yes, Your Majesty!

00:20:13.150 --> 00:20:15.610
I promise, I will come back!

00:20:15.610 --> 00:20:18.860
Mercury, I will leave 
Anders' punishment to you.

00:20:19.230 --> 00:20:22.570
What will you do? He made you lose, Anne.

00:20:25.920 --> 00:20:27.420
Stand up, Jonas.

00:20:29.040 --> 00:20:29.870
Stand up!

00:20:45.520 --> 00:20:47.020
I feel so much better!

00:20:47.020 --> 00:20:49.320
I've been wanting to give him one good hit!

00:20:49.320 --> 00:20:51.850
I like it! A very appropriate measure.

00:20:55.170 --> 00:20:57.310
All right! Then, we're done here!

00:20:59.250 --> 00:21:00.020
I'm sorry.

00:21:01.060 --> 00:21:02.610
Oh, I'm so sorry!

00:21:02.610 --> 00:21:04.390
Pardon me!

00:21:11.650 --> 00:21:13.660
Challe, thank you.

00:21:14.160 --> 00:21:17.320
I couldn't become 
this year's silver sugar master.

00:21:18.140 --> 00:21:21.380
I didn't make it in time 
to send Mama to the heavens.

00:21:22.000 --> 00:21:26.800
But Mama will have to be content with the 
best sugar confection I can make right now.

00:21:27.290 --> 00:21:30.060
And next year, no matter what...

00:21:30.060 --> 00:21:31.140
I will come here again.

00:21:35.050 --> 00:21:36.400
Here.

00:21:36.400 --> 00:21:39.720
As I promised, this sugar 
confection belongs to you, Challe.

00:21:39.720 --> 00:21:40.690
I'm returning it to you.

00:21:42.900 --> 00:21:44.030
It looks unpalatable.

00:21:44.030 --> 00:21:45.280
What?!

00:21:45.280 --> 00:21:47.280
I want something 
made by a silver sugar master,

00:21:47.280 --> 00:21:49.610
a particularly delicious sugar confection.

00:21:49.610 --> 00:21:51.100
W-What's that supposed to mean?

00:21:51.100 --> 00:21:53.280
You're saying this isn't good enough?

00:21:53.280 --> 00:21:57.040
I told you. I wasn't able 
to become a silver sugar master.

00:21:57.040 --> 00:21:58.940
But next year, I'm sure...

00:22:00.930 --> 00:22:02.910
Then I'll have it next year on this day.

00:22:02.910 --> 00:22:04.340
I have no need of one until then.

00:22:04.880 --> 00:22:09.090
Until you become a silver sugar master, 
I will wait with you.

00:22:09.690 --> 00:22:11.970
What? With me?

00:22:13.060 --> 00:22:13.940
Anne.

00:22:14.760 --> 00:22:16.140
<i>That's the first time...</i>

00:22:20.810 --> 00:22:22.480
<i>That's the first time Challe...</i>

00:22:22.890 --> 00:22:24.300
<i>called me by name.</i>

00:22:35.350 --> 00:22:38.730
Hey, did you see that? 
My once-in-a-lifetime, brilliant acting!

00:22:38.730 --> 00:22:39.620
Mithril!

00:22:40.180 --> 00:22:46.010
I'm sorry, Mithril, for thinking, even 
for a second, that you ate my silver sugar.

00:22:46.610 --> 00:22:49.100
Well, that's just how humans are. 
Didn't surprise me.

00:22:49.100 --> 00:22:52.600
And don't shorten my name! 
I'm Mithril Lid Pod!

00:22:52.600 --> 00:22:59.100
But, Mithril Lid Pod, how did you know 
that Jonas stole my sugar confection?

00:22:59.100 --> 00:23:01.230
Were you secretly following us?

00:23:01.230 --> 00:23:04.620
Huh? I was in your cart the whole time.

00:23:04.620 --> 00:23:05.440
What?

00:23:05.440 --> 00:23:07.950
You suspected me. I went to bed in a huff.

00:23:07.950 --> 00:23:10.490
When I woke up, the cart belonged to Jonas.

00:23:11.460 --> 00:23:13.290
S-So that's what happened.

00:23:13.290 --> 00:23:14.950
Just how long were you asleep, anyway?

00:23:15.800 --> 00:23:17.200
Did you forget?

00:23:17.200 --> 00:23:21.230
To repay that favor, I'm gonna follow you 
through sheer stubbornness if I have to.

00:23:21.230 --> 00:23:23.980
I'll follow you to the depths 
of the underworld!

00:23:23.980 --> 00:23:28.550
Have you heard the phrase 
"a helpful nuisance," Mithril Lid Pod?

00:23:28.890 --> 00:23:30.700
I haven't. Sorry.

00:23:30.700 --> 00:23:33.530
And why are you still with Anne?

00:23:33.530 --> 00:23:35.720
There's something 
Scarecrow is going to give me.

00:23:35.720 --> 00:23:39.680
I-I'm Scarecrow again? 
You called me by name earlier.

00:23:40.250 --> 00:23:42.650
What's wrong, Scarecrow? Hurry up and get in.

00:23:42.650 --> 00:23:43.770
Oh, very well!

00:23:43.770 --> 00:23:46.140
I'll let it pass this time, whether 
you call me a scarecrow or a crow!

00:23:46.140 --> 00:23:47.390
Out of the way!

00:23:47.390 --> 00:23:48.650
You're driving?

00:23:48.650 --> 00:23:49.490
That's right!

00:23:51.600 --> 00:23:53.350
That's the sort of mood I'm in!

00:23:58.950 --> 00:24:04.880
The Fate of the Royal Medal

00:24:05.960 --> 00:24:09.880
<b>Anne and the Cat's Sugar Confectionery</b>
